@@ -56,6 +56,14 @@ Database-backed job queue (no Redis):
 
 Recurring tasks are declared in `config/recurring.yml`.
 
+### Storage usage
+
+Accounts and boards keep a running total of the storage they use in their `bytes_used` column, exposed as `Account#bytes_used` and `Board#bytes_used`:
+- Only what people upload counts: card images, and files embedded in board descriptions, card descriptions, and comments. Avatars, image variants, exports and imports don't
+- A board counts everything on it and on its cards; an account counts everything across its boards
+- Totals are kept up to date in the background, applying one delta per attachment as attachments come and go, so reads and writes stay O(1) no matter how much is attached (`StorageUsage`, `StorageAccountable`)
+- `bin/rails storage:recalculate_usage` recalculates every total from scratch, which is also what imports do once their records are in place
+
 ### Sharded Full-Text Search
 
 Full-text search runs in the database, not Elasticsearch. On MySQL it is sharded 16 ways by CRC32 of the account ID (`Search::Record::Trilogy`); on SQLite it is a single FTS5 index (`Search::Record::SQLite`). Don't assume the sharded shape when working under SQLite. Models in `app/models/search/`.
